# Element-wise arithmetic on two growable [T] arrays of DIFFERENT lengths must
# abort cleanly at runtime, naming BOTH lengths. A [T] length is only known at
# run time, so this is the one mismatch the compiler cannot catch; padding the
# short side or truncating the long one would both be a silent wrong answer.
#
# Expected: exit 1 with
#   tycho: element-wise arithmetic on arrays of different lengths (3 and 2)
#
# HISTORY: this fixture lived in tests/postfreeze/abort/ from 2026-07-29 until
# later the same day. `scripts/frontparity.sh` globbed `tests/abort/*.ty` and
# scored "tychoc accepted it, tychoc0 refused it" as a DIVERGENCE; this program
# is post-freeze (tychoc accepts it, the frozen tychoc0 refuses it as a type
# error), so putting it here would have reddened that lane by construction. The
# lane was retired and the fixture came home. tests/run.sh's tests/abort/ loop
# runs it: build with tychoc, run native-only, require a nonzero exit and a
# 'tycho:' message. Native-only because a deliberate exit(1) leaves live arenas
# and LeakSanitizer would report them, correctly and uselessly.

fn main():
    a := [1, 2, 3]
    b := [4, 5]
    println("about to multiply arrays of different lengths")
    println(str(a * b))
